{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting","id":780921,"title":"ex3 Solar shapeshifting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-05T22:15:14-08:00","id":780921,"title":"ex3 Solar shapeshifting","content":"Let me first start i'm not interested in using sorcery to achieve this, i'm pretty sure sorcery could do this but the concept my character is built around doesn't lean towards learning sorcery at all, it is not something I could ever reasonably see this character picking up.<br /> <br /> Would a high tier survival charm be able to pull this off? yes yes I know stepping on lunar toes with this one but my ST is fine with the idea as it very much works in line with my character and how the games developing so far. He did say maybe an armor evocation could do this, but I admit I havent even bothered reading that section, and even so i'd likely still come out being unsure how to make it work.<br /> <br /> I should also clarify by shapeshifting I mean full transformation into an animal, not partial like a lunars DBT, or just growing claws, wings etc. and for long durations of time(indefinatly if its a charm, with commited cost?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:17:21-08:00","id":780924,"title":"","content":"Short answer: nope, not no way, not no how. Closest I think it might come is getting in tune with an animal enough to do something like Game of Thrones-style warging, putting your mind in the animal's body while your body is sleeping or in a trance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:18:29-08:00","id":780927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=780924#post780924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short answer: nope, not no way, not no how. Closest I think it might come is getting in tune with an animal enough to do something like Game of Thrones-style warging, putting your mind in the animal's body while your body is sleeping or in a trance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theres already a survival charm that does JUST that, but really its not a matter of if YOU would personally allow it, I'm looking for ideas as to how to make a charm or evocation for this idea. My ST has given my the FULL go ahead to do this. To each his own though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:25:33-08:00","id":780930,"title":"","content":"I should also add which my ST told me to mention which I forgot! We only want her to be able to turn into ONE animal(a snow lion). Not every single one that would be a bit much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:31:19-08:00","id":780933,"title":"","content":"Solars don't shape shift with native magics. That's not in theme with them. You are going to want to look at artifacts and evocations to pull this off without going out of scope for a Solar.<br /> <br /> What animal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 12-06-2015, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:32:41-08:00","id":780934,"title":"","content":"It's your game, you can do what you like.<br /> <br /> But in canon, it's outside of Solar competence. In fact, that may be one of things <i>explicitly</i> called out as something they can't do. So...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:34:34-08:00","id":780936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=780927#post780927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theres already a survival charm that does JUST that, but really its not a matter of if YOU would personally allow it, I'm looking for ideas as to how to make a charm or evocation for this idea. My ST has given my the FULL go ahead to do this. To each his own though</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends what kind of theme you want to go for.<br /> <br /> An example could be an artifact based on skin-changers : a pelt decorated with Orichalcum and Moonsilver that, when &quot;activated&quot; (a smudge of blood is customary), closes onto its wearer and transforms them into the pelt's respective animal - though this is closer to a main effect rather than an evocation.<br /> <br /> An other alternitive would be Endowment or being the child of an animal diety. The devs have explicitly stated that being a spirit-blooded Exalted allows you to access both power sets, which means transforming into the animal of one's parent's domain is perfectly acceptable for an exalt, it just doesn't come from their exaltation; unless you're Lunar, that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 12-06-2015, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:35:46-08:00","id":780937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=780934#post780934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's your game, you can do what you like.<br /> <br /> But in canon, it's outside of Solar competence. In fact, that may be one of things <i>explicitly</i> called out as something they can't do. So...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah but we are not really running fully in cannon, its a solo game we experiment with stuff we wouldnt do in group games or even begin to allow for a group. Such as taking the rules and smashing them to bits when it comes to &quot;you cant do this cause [insert reason here]. We play to have fun, if it fits the concept, and is resonable, the ST will let it happen. <br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure you are right though cannon likely says no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:39:32-08:00","id":780942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=780936#post780936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends what kind of theme you want to go for.<br /> <br /> An example could be an artifact based on skin-changers : a pelt decorated with Orichalcum and Moonsilver that, when &quot;activated&quot; (a smudge of blood is customary), closes onto its wearer and transforms them into the pelt's respective animal - though this is closer to a main effect rather than an evocation.<br /> <br /> An other alternitive would be Endowment or being the child of an animal diety. The devs have explicitly stated that being a spirit-blooded Exalted allows you to access both power sets, which means transforming into the animal of one's parent's domain is perfectly acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like that first idea as does my ST, though he just told me if we use that he'd not allow acsess to the animals abilites it would be cosmetic only, and use my stats as normal. He said anything more would be to much. It is good to know we have a line though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:53:20-08:00","id":780946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=780942#post780942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> He said anything more would be too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on its rating, as it seems, to me at least, that merely having a cosmetic change is pretty low on the power scale. It changes how people react to you (mostly for the worse, as people don't take kindly to stray predators in their town), which is basically a mere disguise.<br /> <br /> I don't know what you'd want to rate it at, but at 4 I'd probably make it at least as useful as a god's shapeshifting power; and at 5 add an evocation or two (it's a pretty front-loaded item though, so evocations would be few and mostly utilitarian, if any.) Because at 5 we're talking about legendary artifacts that have legacies that outlive their owners, and a cosmetic appearance change is more on the level of &quot;trick&quot; than &quot;legendary treasure&quot;. <br /> <br /> Anyway, it's not my game, so you may take this as the tired mutterings of a grognard ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:55:52-08:00","id":780949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=780946#post780946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on its rating, as it seems, to me at least, that merely having a cosmetic change is pretty low on the power scale. It changes how people react to you (mostly for the worse, as people don't take kindly to stray predators in their town), which is basically a mere disguise.<br /> <br /> I don't know what you'd want to rate it at, but at 4 I'd probably make it at least as useful as a god's shapeshifting power; and at 5 add an evocation or two (it's a pretty front-loaded item though, so evocations would be few and mostly utilitarian, if any.) Because at 5 we're talking about legendary artifacts that have legacies that outlive their owners, and a cosmetic appearance change is more on the level of &quot;trick&quot; than &quot;legendary treasure&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's not my game, so you may take this as the tired mutterings of a grognard ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tired mutterings or not I find it helpful and am going to pass it over to my ST to consider! I think its a good idea, and likely fits what we are looking for without being &quot;to much&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T22:56:13-08:00","id":780950,"title":"","content":"An Eclipse could potentially learn a Spirit Charm that allowed it. Otherwise... Hmm... might be able to pull it off with that Integrity Charm that lets you take power from a gods purview. Divine Mantle, that's it. Otherwise I personally would say native to Solars charms are out, though in the game you've mentioned I could see it as a survival charm that keys off the one that lets you put your mind in an animal's body. I don't know what Essence that charm is, but I would put it as one Essence higher, unless it's already Essence 5 (though as you suggested Survival, I'm already guessing Survival Supernal).<br /> <br /> Edit: Seems you like the artifact idea someone else posted. It works well and is thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","user":"Bulshock","date":". 12-06-2015, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T23:31:43-08:00","id":780960,"title":"","content":"you could have the character have an artifact that allows her to do it, i'm thinking something from her previous incarnation that was made in memory of her lunar mate that mimicked their primary shape change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T00:57:19-08:00","id":780998,"title":"","content":"If you just want the look, you can do it with larceny as a disguise. Add some athletics for speed, jump etc... voila you are a snow fox.<br /> <br /> If you want to assume the form literally, you need a moonsilver artifact. God-Blood route has already been explained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T05:34:49-08:00","id":781082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scelesta</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a high tier survival charm be able to pull this off?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think if you're going to make it an unintrusive part of the Solar milieu, you'd be better off just making it a low-key thing. Maybe not an entry Charm, but not many steps up. If it was going to be high tier, I think it should carry a bit more weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T06:16:16-08:00","id":781098,"title":"","content":"I would allow it to be an entry charm for an Eclipse, and I would tweak the shapeshifting power of the Neomah until everyone's satisfied.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Bold\"><b>Snow Lion Form </b><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\">(4m; Simple; One scene; Eclipse;Essence 1)<br /> Gain the form of a snow lion. Gain the Mauling Bite special attack (p.566) as well as the Camouflage and Night Vision merits (p.566). Attributes and abilities remain the same. Claws are light weapons with the Lethal, Brawl and Natural tags, and the Bite is a medium weapon with Lethal, Grappling, Brawl and Natural tags.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T07:34:43-08:00","id":781128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=781098#post781098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow it to be an entry charm for an Eclipse, and I would tweak the shapeshifting power of the Neomah until everyone's satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd base it on Fakharu's Clothed in Humanity power, personally (but in reverse) -- 5m, simple, but it's one form, and (seems to be) always the same one.<br /> Also of note: one cannot use Martial Arts or Melee Charms effectively in animal form (unless your ST is okay with you weilding a Daiklave with your mouth), so there is a somewhat balancing tradeoff there.<br /> <br /> Also, as potentially interesting fluff re: pelt - damage taken while donning it is reflected on it as scars and holes, and heals at normal rates; though actual scars and crippling injuries remain unless healed/restored with magic. In short, it's not the form of *a* (e.g.) Snow Leopard. It's the form of *the* legendary Snow Leopard Agloolik, who walked in ice, ran tracelessly as the wind through snow and tricked the Aurorae Borealis to shine gold in the east. [then some stuff happened, can't decide what]; Upon its death, it was immortalised as an artifact by one of the (Lunar?) Exalted such that its legacy would live on through anyone who wears its pelt.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this makes it much easier to come up with Evocations for it.<br /> <br /> Dammit, now I want to put this in my game... *scrambles to shift narrative elements around, searching for an opening*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T08:42:48-08:00","id":781151,"title":"","content":"Tattoo artifact with evocations imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T08:45:45-08:00","id":781153,"title":"","content":"I'd probably go with an artifact pelt thing. I don't consider it to be within the Solar wheelhouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:54:59-08:00","id":781357,"title":"","content":"Or maybe some kind of mask.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://1.bp.blogspot.com/-Ue4fYt07MOA/VKtMo8zeR5I/AAAAAAAAAoQ/rLQZ_PV9VeU/s1600/tumblr_mnh9hfWB3G1sps423o1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T15:59:07-08:00","id":781359,"title":"","content":"Why are you on a Majora's Mask gif spree? And since when is that a thing?<br /> <br /> (Not that I <i>mind</i>. It's probably my favourite Zelda, after all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T16:04:26-08:00","id":781364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=781359#post781359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you on a Majora's Mask gif spree? And since when is that a thing?<br /> <br /> (Not that I <i>mind</i>. It's probably my favourite Zelda, after all.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It took me forever to find a &quot;vanishing&quot;-type gif, then suddenly Zelda came to me and struck me with inspiration :P<br /> Incidentally, it's <i>also </i>my favorite. Those transformation scenes are pretty visceral even by today's standards. You can just <i>feel </i>the pain of bones shifting under his face (along with those cracks in the sound effects). That animation and those expressions are <i>so good</i>.<br /> <br /> IMO it's a good way of presenting Shapeshifting when someone not &quot;designed&quot; for it does it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T18:38:34-08:00","id":781455,"title":"","content":"If you're ST is fine with it, then they're fine with it. Survival is as good a place to put it as anything else.<br /> <br /> If you want to try and do it in a way that is at least somewhat &quot;canonically&quot; acceptable, it's harder. The most basic options are:<br /> <br /> 1. Sorcery or Sorcerous Workings. You said you didn't want Sorcery, yes, but I'd suggest you consider Sorcerous Workings. You don't even need to perform them yourself; you can find a Sorcerer somewhere who performs a big ritual where you wear a wolf-pelt under the light of the full moon while he chants arcane runes from the forging of the world, and bam, after that you can turn into a wolf. This is probably the simplest way to get shapeshifting &quot;inherently&quot;. Sorcerous Workings can do just about anything, and &quot;the old man of the mountain imbued me with the spirit of an animal so I can take its shape&quot; is a natural concept for a Sorcerous Working.<br /> <br /> 2. Evocations. You mentioned armor evocations; cloaks of animal feathers or fur that allow you to take on their shapes are also mythologically appropriate and appear in a lot of settings. (If you <i>had</i> to do it as a Solar charm, perhaps you could base it off of this -- a Craft or Occult charm that lets you bring out the power of such garments to assume their form. It somewhat fits within Craft and Occult in that respect, although usually you'd do it by actually making an artifact or performing a sorcerous working.)<br /> <br /> 3. There's a Solar charm in Integrity that lets you gain the charms of a god you champion (or defeat.) Be the champion of a wolf-god. Gain the charm he uses to turn into a wolf as part of his blessings. Or defeat a wolf-god in order to gain his power, either way. An Eclipse could also do it without this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 12-06-2015, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T20:41:58-08:00","id":781514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/780921-ex3-solar-shapeshifting?p=781098#post781098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow it to be an entry charm for an Eclipse, and I would tweak the shapeshifting power of the Neomah until everyone's satisfied.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Bold\"><b>Snow Lion Form </b><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\">(4m; Simple; One scene; Eclipse;Essence 1)<br /> Gain the form of a snow lion. Gain the Mauling Bite special attack (p.566) as well as the Camouflage and Night Vision merits (p.566). Attributes and abilities remain the same. Claws are light weapons with the Lethal, Brawl and Natural tags, and the Bite is a medium weapon with Lethal, Grappling, Brawl and Natural tags.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Four motes? If you're going to keep Lunars as the best at turning into beasts, you should charge Solars out the nose for animal forms. Say, ten motes and one Willpower point (or more), with far fewer options for what they can turn into, if you really, really want Solars turning into animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T21:20:11-08:00","id":781535,"title":"","content":"Get a Snow Lion familiar and use <b>Shadow Replacement Technique</b> (Cost: 8m, 1wp; Mins: Stealth 5, Essence 3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:05:49-08:00","id":781778,"title":"","content":"I second all of Aquilion's suggestions.<br /> Workings done by others, paid for by you, might end up getting you to your goal without costing any more than a favored charm.<br /> Alternatively, Divine Mantle, p. 310, you don't even have to get chummy with the god. If need be, you can go beat him up.<br /> <br /> Either of these might result in interesting play that sheds light on your character as he achieves this power.<br /> <br /> But if you simply want to start with this, and you're fine to lose out on their story potential (or put it off until a later point), I wouldn't see any problem of starting with a working already affecting you, for example.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}